    "created_at": "2016-12-22T18:44:43Z",
    "updated_at": "2016-12-22T19:29:48Z",
    "body": "Granted, this scenario is edge-casey enough that I'm also fine leaving this undefined in the spec -- to allow UAs to do whatever they think is rational, for the brief period of time while the first few bytes of the image are being decoded.\r\n\r\nMy chief concern here is whether the Acid3 test is justified in its expectations here (I don't think it is), or if we have good reason to adjust the test to wait for the image to be complete (so that it's actually testing well-specced behavior).\r\n\r\n(For now, the testcase seems to expect that we take the `If the element represents an image` branch of [this spec-text](https://html.spec.whatwg.org/multipage/rendering.html#images-3), in this scenario where the image really `represents nothing` while its data is being decoded off-main-thread. And I don't see any spec justification for that test-expectation. To be fair, I don't think the test's assumption is intentional - it's most-likely that that all tested browsers simply did their data-URI-decoding synchronously back when the test was written.)",
